# ⚠️  DO NOT PUT SECRETS IN THIS FILE. ⚠️
#
# ShadowBit NEVER persists recovery keys or passwords to disk. Recovery keys
# are shown exactly once (at create / regenerate time) and are stored only
# inside the .vault file, as an encrypted copy of the master key — never in
# plaintext. See SECURITY.md.
#
# There is therefore intentionally NO RECOVERY_KEY variable here. An earlier
# version of this template invited you to store a recovery key in plaintext;
# do NOT do that — it would defeat the entire security model. If you need a
# key that was mislaid, regenerate it instead:
#
#     shadow-bit recovery-key <vault>      # new key (invalidates the old)
#
# This file exists only as a placeholder for tooling that expects a .env. Keep
# it empty, or add only genuinely non-secret, machine-local settings that are
# never committed.